 {:db/id "q-134157" :question/id #uuid "8a0c5df7-a954-59db-a5d6-801a9cd38bf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-134157" :question/problem "A motorcyclist covers $99$ miles in $3$ hours at a constant rate.  What is the speed of the motorcyclist?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed (in miles per hour), we divide the number of miles, $99,$ by the number of hours, $3.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{99}{3}=99÷3=33.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the motorcyclist is $33$ miles per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134157/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88babe91-d8bf-53ba-8d72-35ad35f9253e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134157"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134172/selection/3fe6dbad2958cd1210fbb6cedb3beb54de94b23057fb5280091b75ce572c4296" :answer/id #uuid "cc20bdd8-f392-5169-b9f2-162fa2d2c805" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$150.5$ feet per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134172/selection/c5f1f07959ea6e718139cfff0d2d48d0d06a1474fc965c08e68e1b94fab8dcbb" :answer/id #uuid "cad21f0c-d50a-5b19-b29a-8423801bd390" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$145$ feet per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134172/selection/3057ea07a23e29f14f9f4ed377114d230d464e8241c3ea04232e023734a739c1" :answer/id #uuid "b9f3f5b8-c9f6-57ab-a3b6-739a5818e7cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$132.5$ feet per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134172/selection/f061f86bd431d8dbbe251d8740671bd518b42c72e4e4340a4ff4ab5056264c29" :answer/id #uuid "3ba1d00d-cdf4-5d6a-922a-720486e52722" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$301$ feet per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134172/selection/ef0f9737cca28db6