9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the peregrine falcon covers $119$ meters in $7$ seconds." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134182/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "534de76f-d4bc-55b5-858e-2b594f63b7bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134182"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-133998"] :question/worked-solution "The speed is $55$ miles per hour. To find the distance covered in $3$ hours, we multiply the speed by $3.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\cdot \\text{time} \\\\  & =55\\times 3 \\\\  & =165.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the car covered $165$ miles in $3$ hours." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-133999"] :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in meters per minute, we divide the number of meters, $190,$ by the number of minutes, $2.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{190}{2} & =190÷2 \\\\  & =95.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the person is $95$ meters per minute. \n\nTo find the distance covered in $5$ minutes, we multiply the speed by $5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\times \\text{time} \\\\  & =95\\times 5 \\\\  & =475.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the person can cover $475$ meters in $5$ minutes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-134243/selection/baf48cf97f0c681864d407163167403d6b26e601eedeb370f06535fa079ba104" :answer/id #uuid "934135c8-6757-5991-ae58-f01df37cf4ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$90$ centimeters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134243/selection/e0810af