on/id #uuid "164076ec-371c-50b4-a03b-6cac29c4e58c" :question/math-academy-id "q-134238" :question/problem "It takes $4$ hours for a marathon runner to run $20$ miles at a constant pace. How long does it take for the marathon runner to run $26$ miles?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in miles per hour, we divide the number of miles, which is $20,$ by the number of hours, $4.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20}{4} & =20÷4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the marathon runner is $5$ miles per hour. \n\nTo find the time it takes the marathon runner to cover $26$ miles, we divide the distance by $5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{5} \\\\  & =26÷5 \\\\  & =5.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the marathon runner $5.2$ hours to run $26$ miles." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134238/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6570253a-b05a-5721-9108-5fddab2b5388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134238"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134241/selection/dfe3bab4b43f6fd110a87f830b12da6f4305e4550293b412d89ca1f670f9d78f" :answer/id #uuid "8d099903-6b3e-5c24-aab4-76aa1055baa4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$52$ seconds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134241/selection/9a49e21fc94c07705064a5313e53802fd629241d8ff67233a93538cb51d155e1" :answer/id #uuid "25c1253b-b52c-5124-8078-a19691b7d875" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$40$ seconds" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134241/selection/c53023d1816d3df0a93a51e0be4d4fd2ba476bd719d805d4415dd31865601d2e" :answer/id #uuid "193aad1c-839a-58f4-bb42-b3b48f45df60" :answer/type :answer.t